Z||000000||86_Fastback||09-20-2000||09:35 AM||||I hav been chasing a high idle at start up for a while now and need some help.  At start-up, idle is about 2600-2800 rpm.  After about 30 seconds or so, the idle drops, almost stalls and then idles normal (1100-1200 rpm cold 1000-900 rpm warm).  Every once in a while if the car is warm at start-up, the service engine light will come on.  I have not been able to grab codes when the light is on, but afterwards I have gotten an IAC fault.  Replaced IAC valve same proble.  Replaced TPS sensor and check linkage, same problem.  <BR>Last night replaced MAP sensor.  The car started up with idle around 1500 rpm, but after about 15-20 seconds the car stalled.  Re-started fine, but stalled 15-20 seconds later.  This happens again and again.  Put old MAP sensor in, and car starts and runs as before.  Anyone have any ideas?<P>Gregg<P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
